Loads **turing_unlock** ([nlzy/turing-unlock](https://github.com/nlzy/turing-unlock)) at boot, before the nvidia-driver plugin loads `nvidia`.
It unlocks the full FP16 tensor-core rate of NVIDIA Turing cards, primarily the TU102 **RTX 2080 Ti** (`10de:1e07`).
Dense FP16 GEMM (LLM prefill, diffusion) gets faster; memory-bound work (LLM decode) does not.

The module must run before `nvidia` binds the card, so **settings take effect at the next boot**. The plugin ships an
`/etc/rc.d/rc.modules-<kernel>` hook; if the module is already loaded, nothing changes until a reboot.

