### Firmware

The plugin release includes the pinned 610.43.03 firmware package, and the plugin installs it automatically. If it
is missing or you want to rebuild it, this action downloads the pinned inputs from NVIDIA/CachyOS on this machine,
verifies their SHA-256, and packs the package locally. It needs `python3`, `zstd`, about 1 GB of free space and
several minutes.

<form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="/plugins/<?=$plugin?>/scripts/gpu-turing-unlock">
<input type="hidden" name="#arg[1]" value="firmware">
: <input type="submit" value="Rebuild firmware package">
</form>

> After it finishes, reboot so the module loads with the firmware in place.

### Unraid updates

An Unraid OS update changes the kernel, and a `turing_unlock.ko` built for the old kernel will not
load. The plugin watches `/boot/changes.txt`; when an update is staged it reads the kernel the new
OS will boot and downloads the matching module package (with its SHA-256) from the latest release
to the flash, so `rc.modules` installs it on the first boot of the new kernel. If the release has no
module for that kernel yet, you get a notification instead and the cards stay at the stock rate.

<form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="/plugins/<?=$plugin?>/scripts/gpu-turing-unlock">
<input type="hidden" name="#arg[1]" value="post-update">
: <input type="submit" value="Check for the pending kernel's module">
</form>

> This only downloads the package. The module is installed and loaded at the next boot, before
> `nvidia`.

